  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, a self-employed individual with gross sales below ₱3 million can opt for the 8% income tax rate, provided their gross sales or gross receipts do not exceed the VAT threshold of ₱3 million.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe relevant provision is found in Section 24 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which allows self-employed individuals and professionals to choose an 8% tax rate on gross sales or gross receipts exceeding ₱250,000 in lieu of the graduated income tax rates.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor self-employed individuals, this means that if their gross sales are below ₱3 million and above ₱250,000, they can simplify their tax obligations by opting for the 8% income tax rate instead of the more complex graduated tax rates. This can lead to easier compliance and potentially lower tax liabilities, depending on their specific income levels.",
